  "problem": "Which of the following pairs of sets are disjoint?\n\n- ${3,4,5}$ and ${6,7,8}$\n- ${-4,-3,-2}$ and ${2,3,4}$\n- $[-3,0]$ and $[0,3]$",
  "worked_solution": "Two sets $A$ and $B$ are *disjoint* if they have no element in common, i.e., their intersection is empty:\n\n$$\nA\\cap B=\u2205\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Pair I is disjoint. Indeed, the intersection of the sets is empty:\n\n$$\n{3,4,5}\\cap {6,7,8}=\u2205\\,\\,\u2713\n$$\n\n- Pair II is also disjoint. Indeed, the intersection of the sets is empty:\n\n$$\n{-4,-3,-2}\\cap {2,3,4}=\u2205\\,\\,\u2713\n$$\n\n- Pair III is *not* disjoint since the intersection of the sets is not empty:\n\n$$\n[-3,0]\\cap [0,3]={0}\\ne \u2205\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
